\section*{P=W for fixed-determinant trace-free coprime moduli}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For fixed determinant and trace-free Higgs moduli in coprime composite rank, OpenAI claims equality of the perverse and weight filtrations on the full rational cohomology, completing all coprime ranks with known cases. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Let $C$ be a complex curve, smooth and projective, with genus $g\ge2$, composite $n\ge4$, $\gcd(n,d)=1$, and $L\in\operatorname{Pic}^d(C)$. Let $X$ parametrize stable rank-$n$, determinant-$L$, trace-free Higgs bundles, with Hitchin map $h:X\to A=\bigoplus_{i=2}^nH^0(C,K_C^i)$ and $R=(n^2-1)(g-1)$. The corresponding Betti variety is
\[
X^B=\{(A_j,B_j)\in\operatorname{SL}_n(\mathbb C)^{2g}:\prod_j[A_j,B_j]=e^{2\pi id/n}I\}\mathbin{/\mkern-6mu/}\operatorname{SL}_n.
\]
Transport the perverse filtration $P_kH^m(X)=\operatorname{im}[H^{m-R}(A,{}^p\tau_{\le k}Rh_*\mathbb Q_X[R])\to H^m(X)]$ by nonabelian Hodge theory. OpenAI claims
\[
P_kH^m(X^B,\mathbb Q)=W_{2k}H^m(X^B,\mathbb Q)=W_{2k+1}H^m(X^B,\mathbb Q)
\]
for every $m,k\ge0$, where $W$ is Deligne's weight filtration. The determinant is fixed and the composite-rank coprime-degree restrictions are part of the theorem.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 043, 2026-09-24): Determinant-root covers transfer toric stratifications and establish curious hard Lefschetz beyond the invariant summand. Finite algebraic-fiber diagrams carry the required weight-zero moving-base cochains, furnishing lowering operators compatible with the full cohomology and the common Lie-algebra structure.

